      <marc:subfield code="a">Datuk A. Samad Said is a Malaysian poet and novelist who, in May 1976, was named by Malay literature communities and many of the country&apos;s linguists as the Pejuang Sastera (Literary Exponent) receiving, within the following decade, the 1979 Southeast Asia Write Award and, in 1986, in appreciation of his continuous writings and contributions to the nation&apos;s literary heritage, or Kesusasteraan Melayu, the title Sasterawan Negara.</marc:subfield>
